            <ArticleTitle>Modification of the modified condylotomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>548-51; discussion 551-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This article describes the results of modification of the condylotomy procedure for treating painful internal derangements of the temporomandibular joint.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Data on postoperative disc position, joint space, and pain were evaluated in patients who underwent either the original modified condylotomy or the newly modified procedure.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Less anterior and inferior sag of the condyle was produced by the new technique. Pain relief and disc reduction were about the same with both procedures.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The new modifications make the operation quicker and easier, while producing outcomes similar to those obtained with the original modified procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
